        <p>Evan Thomas Evans—proposed and seconded by Thomas Clare and David Forrester.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-03-28_WidnesExaminer_art0078" n="art0078">
        <head>VIADUCT WARD.</head>
        <p>VIADUCT WARD.</p>
        <p>Alfred Tunstall—proposed and seconded by George Stargess and C. Charlton.</p>
        <p>WARGRAVE WARD.</p>
        <p>. _ William Thompson—proposed and seconded by Edward Cadogan Turner and W. W. Thompson.</p>
        <p>LOCAL MUSICIANS AT PRESTON. An interesting programme was furnished by the following local artistes at a concert given at Leyland near Preston on Saturday last :—Soprano, Miss Alice Rigby ; contralto, Miss Etta Bodruer, L.L.C.M. silver medalist of the Zurich Conservatoire ; baritone, Mr. T. Finney; solo violinist, Mr. Noah Augustus Rigby, gold,silver and bronze medalist ; solo pianist and accompanist, Mr. Edward J. Rigby. Miss Alice Rigby gave excellent renderings of her songs and her delightful soprano voice and artistic taste greatly added to the charm of her songs,gaining double encores. Miss Bodmer whose contralto voice is of such a rich quality showed refinement and good taste in her items, being twice recalled. Miss Bodmer is very well known locally. Mr. Finney is a baritone of promise and well merited his encores. Mr. Noah Rigby a violinist whose reputation is now so well estab- lished, showed a perfect mastery over the technical difficulties in which the violin abounds. A continuous round of applause greeted his first item which was one of his own arrangements and in response he played with consummate skill and taste Dvorak's Humourousque. Miss Bodmer later in the programme joined Mr. Noah and Edward Rigby in an instrumental trio in which the ensemble was very fine. Mr. Edward Rigby acted as a very able and efficient accompanist. The local press speak very highly of the standard of excellence reached by each of the artistes.</p>
      </div>
