        <p>The arrangements for the demonstration promoted by the Warrington Citizens' Temperance League in support of the Bill, which will be held in the Parr flail on Friday, April 10th, are now complete. The chief speakers will be the Bishop of Liverpool, gr. Charles Roberts. NI. P., (Lincoln), and Mr. W. Nladden. Ntr. James Dodds (president of the League) will preside. Before the meeting begins, selections will be rendered by the Band of Elope choir._</p>
        <p>The " A. " team was very strongly represented against Wigan Highfield, but they lost 6-3. Isherwood</p>
