        <p>Fnw—On :Icarch 22nd, at her residence 15, London-rd., Stockton Heath, Ann, wife of Mr. Alfred Few, nett; 80 years. WAZSON.—Suddenly at Llandudno, on the 24th of, March, Agnes, the beloved and only daughter of Johtti Watson, of 3, Wilson Patten-street, Warrington. Interment to-day (Saturday) at Broughty Ferry, N.B.</p>
        <p>Pr{ Btal Rai</p>
        <p>A horror came to me one night, A spectre blear and old— " Your name ! " I cried in wild affright. It said, " I am a cold." "Begone !" I cried. "Your clammy touch Twill no more endure ! " And straight it vanished at the sight Of Woods' Groat Peppermint Cure.—Advt.</p>
